### 5.5 Scale for the QCD Phase Diagram

Lattice QCD results for \(\kappa\sigma^{2}\) and \(S\sigma\) are obtained for dimensionless parameters \(T/T_{c}\) and \(\mu_{B}/T\), where \(T_{c}\) is the transition temperature at \(\mu_{B}=0\). For a given value of energy (\(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\rm NN}}}\)), the experimental observables are calculated at the corresponding chemical freeze-out, characterized by \(T\) and \(\mu_{B}\). Thus, comparison of experiment and theory requires a choice of the scale, \(T_{c}\). By varying this scale to obtain the best fit between the QCD predications and the experimental measurements, we are able to determine the \(T_{c}\). This is the first direct comparison between results from a heavy ion experiment and lattice QCD of strongly

